      "explanation": "The credited endpoint is now defined: for a nonempty request it is req.Entries[len-1].Index; empty requests produce no match report. Both ordinary and pipeline success consumers call the same helper. Ordinary rejection backtracks nextIndex, while pipeline sends advance a separate speculative send index and decoding stops on an unsuccessful response. Request construction reads the prefix from a log or snapshot and entries from the leader's LogStore. These dependencies constrain the suspected sequence but do not establish its reachability.",
